I've written two task files and the issue responses for this session (task_01.md, task_02.md, issue_responses.md). The commit didn't happen: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused it. The files are on disk for the harness to read, but they aren't committed.

Task 1: Fixes #1057. The /spawn stale-worktree sweep stops deleting worktrees that belong to --bg workers that are still running.
• The bug: the sweep removes any clean worktree whose top folder hasn't changed for an hour. A background worker that hasn't written anything yet looks clean, so its working directory can disappear mid-task.
• The fix: the spawn tracker records each worker's worktree path. The sweep's decision moves into a pure function that takes the set of live paths as an argument, so tests can drive it directly.
• Tests: a table pins the cases, including "old and clean but not live is still swept" so today's behaviour isn't lost. A deliberate break of the live check must turn a test red.
• Leftover: this doesn't protect a worker owned by a different yoyo process. The task says to file that as its own issue before pushing, so "Fixes" stays true.
• Why this one: spawn is outside main, which the trajectory flagged. Claude Code just shipped a fix for the same kind of bug.

Task 2: Fixes #1062. This is the backlog-drain slot. Of the 23 open self-filed issues, this one has the least work left.
• What's left: the 401-hint half was fixed in 9eff971c. The remaining half is that a key passed with --api-key still opens the first-run setup wizard.
• The fix: needs_setup_from gets an input saying whether the command line supplied a key, with a table test for each key source. An empty --api-key "" counts as no key, and having no key anywhere must still open the wizard.
• Where the key info comes from: the task says to take it from the parsed arguments, not from the global that's switched off under tests.
• Check: a before/after run of the real binary in a terminal, pasted into the commit.

